ype":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot v4.5.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.stable - Windows 10 (build 19045) \n\n### Issue description\n\nUsing `load()` or `ResourceLoader.load()` in thread will allow subsequent code to obtain nodes in the scene tree\n\nIf it is for performance or not a bug, I think we should add some explanation to the documentation.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/de950bc2-805d-4059-9025-af6f9c3926a0)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nNew Scene -> Add Script -> Add Child\n```\nextends Node2D\n\nvar thread\n\nfunc _ready():\n    thread = Thread.new()\n    thread.start(thread1_function)\n\nfunc thread1_function():\n    ResourceLoader.load(\"res://icon.svg\")\n    print(JSON.stringify(get_children(), \"\\t\"))\n    Thread.set_thread_safety_checks_enabled(true)\n    print(JSON.stringify(get_children(), \"\\t\"))\n\nfunc _exit_tree():\n    thread.wait_to_finish()\n\n```\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110739/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110739/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}